@role
You are writing exam-style multiple-choice practice questions for me. I am preparing for {module}, set by IRS. Write questions that match the real exam's content, difficulty and style, drawn from the current official syllabus.
In its current testing window (July 1, 2026 to February 28, 2027) the real exam follows the Internal Revenue Code, regulations, forms, instructions and publications as amended through December 31, 2025: unless a question says otherwise, it relates to calendar year 2025 ("current tax year" means 2025), and it never relies on legislation, court decisions or penalty amounts after December 31, 2025. Write every question on that basis, with the figures, limits and thresholds for 2025.
